  "pr_title": "docs(docs): record the 0.1.0 release in the changelog",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nThe changelog has a 0.1.0 section, so the release workflow can publish the first release of spsync.\n\n## Summary\n\n`CHANGELOG.md` moves the Unreleased entries under `## [0.1.0] - 2026-11-11` and adds an empty Unreleased section. The 0.1.0 entries also say that each release publishes the source archive of the build. Link definitions for Unreleased and 0.1.0 follow Keep a Changelog. The three manifests already declare version 0.1.0, so no version change is necessary. The change does not touch docx reading or patching.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `scripts/release_notes.py 0.1.0` prints the 0.1.0 section and stops before the link definitions.\n- `scripts/check_versions.py --expect 0.1.0` passes.\n- The `v0.0.1` test release from a throwaway branch passed every workflow step. The release had the five files. The checksum matched, the extracted CLI printed `spsync 0.0.1`, and `spsync doctor --json` ran. The test release, the tag, and the branch are deleted.\n\n## Issue\n\nRefs #5\n"
}